  },
  "derivation": {
    "raw_object_count": 152,
    "banner_filter": {
      "field": "banner_type",
      "equals": "character_event"
    },
    "selected_banner_count": 74,
    "pity_fields": "5star_pity1 through 5star_pity90",
    "sample_unit": "One aggregated count of a recorded five-star character appearing at a given pity value. It is neither the total number of wishes nor a count of unique players.",
    "total_five_star_hit_records": 22047495,
    "count_definition": "count[n] = sum(row['5star_pity<n>']) over rows where banner_type == 'character_event'",
    "at_risk_definition": "at_risk[n] = sum(count[k] for k = n..90)",
    "estimated_conditional_q_definition": "estimated_q[n] = count[n] / at_risk[n], assuming each recorded completed waiting interval is observable from its reset point"
  },
  "caveats": [
    "The source is a self-selected sample of players who used Paimon.moe and submitted wish records, not a random sample of all players.",
    "Imported histories may begin at nonzero pity or omit older records. Left truncation, missing history, and unfinished waits can bias early-pity rates and the mean.",
    "estimated_conditional_q reconstructs its denominator from tail counts and does not correct for left truncation or right censoring. It is only a community-record estimate.",
    "A CDF made by normalizing these hit counts describes the cumulative share among recorded five-star hits; it is not automatically an exact from-zero player CDF.",
    "The aggregate mixes 74 character-event banners and multiple game versions. It supports a broad shape, not a claim that the server-side formula never changed.",
    "Counts become sparse after pity 84, and estimated_conditional_q becomes visibly noisy. q[90] equals one by construction and the hard limit.",
    "The fields contain only five-star arrival pity. They cannot identify guarantee state, Capturing Radiance history, or whether the result was the featured character.",
    "Video labeling should say community-submitted-record estimate, not official per-pull formula, and keep official values, community fits, and teaching illustrations distinct."
  ],
